---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StudyGraphic from './StudyGraphic.astro';
import EvidenceExhibit from './EvidenceExhibit.astro';
import WorkLibrary from './WorkLibrary.astro';
import {type DesignStudy,studyTitle} from '../data/design-studies';
import {getProjects} from '../data/content';
import '../styles/work-library.css';
interface Props {study:DesignStudy;}
const {study}=Astro.props;
const projects=await getProjects();
const structuredStudy={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CreativeWork',name:studyTitle(study),description:study.description,url:'https://nrth.group/work/'+study.slug,dateCreated:study.date,dateModified:study.reviewedAt,creator:{'@type':'Organization',name:'NRTH Inc.',url:'https://nrth.group'},about:[{'@type':'Thing',name:study.subject},{'@type':'Thing',name:study.field}],creativeWorkStatus:'Published illustrative website design study',hasPart:{'@type':'CreativeWork',name:study.artifact.type,url:'https://nrth.group'+study.artifact.href}};
const inquiryHref='/contact?project='+study.ventures[0]+'&topic='+encodeURIComponent('Design study: '+studyTitle(study));
---
<Layout title={studyTitle(study)} description={study.description}>
 <script type='application/ld+json' set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredStudy).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')}/>
 <section class='study-heading'><span class='section-label'>A documented NRTH design study</span><h1 set:html={study.title}/><p>{study.subtitle} {study.description}</p><div class='study-kicker'><span>{study.subject}</span><time datetime={study.date}>Recorded 12 October 2026</time><span>Illustrative website design work</span></div></section>
 <section class='study-overview'><StudyGraphic kind={study.kind} title={studyTitle(study)}/><div><span class='section-label'>The question</span><h2>{study.question}</h2><p>The artifact is available to inspect. Its record explains what was made, the choices behind it and the review that would be needed before extending the idea.</p><a class='inline-link' href={study.artifact.href}>{study.artifact.label}</a><p class='study-overview-scope'>This record documents an implemented creative interface. Synthetic states are examples, and the work reports no customer, clinical, laboratory or event outcomes.</p></div></section>
 <nav class='study-section-nav' aria-label='Study sections'><a href='#context'>The context</a><a href='#method'>The method</a><a href='#artifact'>Inspect the example</a><a href='#scope'>Support and limits</a><a href='#review'>Review and resources</a></nav>
 <section class='study-section' id='context'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>The idea<br/>in its setting.</h2><p>A specific design question, with the wider context still in view.</p></div><div class='study-introduction'>{study.introduction.map(text=><p>{text}</p>)}</div></section>
 <section class='study-section section-dark' id='method'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>How the<br/><em>study is framed.</em></h2><p>The method records the authored choices and the conditions that matter to the example.</p></div><div class='study-method-grid'>{study.method.map(item=><article><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class='study-section section-dark study-exhibits' id='artifact'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>Change the context.<br/><em>Examine the difference.</em></h2><p>Compare the two states. The orange path marks relationships with context in place; unresolved connections remain open.</p></div>{study.exhibits.map(exhibit=><EvidenceExhibit exhibit={exhibit}/>)}<a class='inline-link' href={study.artifact.href}>{study.artifact.label}</a></section>
 <section class='study-section' id='observations'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>What the artifact<br/>makes visible.</h2><p>These descriptions concern the authored interface. They are not reported results from an external investigation.</p></div><div class='study-observation-grid'>{study.observations.map(item=><article><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class='study-section' id='scope'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>A useful claim<br/>has a boundary.</h2><p>Keep the question attached to what this particular artifact can support.</p></div><div class='study-record'><div><h3>What it supports</h3><ul>{study.supports.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ul></div><div><h3>What it does not establish</h3><ul>{study.limits.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ul></div></div></section>
 <section class='study-section' id='review'><div class='study-section-heading'><h2>Take the question<br/>into your context.</h2><p>Use the review as a starting point. Bring descriptions or redacted examples you are able to share.</p></div><ol class='study-review-list'>{study.nextReview.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ol><div class='study-downloads'><a href={'/resources/studies/'+study.slug+'-worksheet.txt'} download>Download the study worksheet</a><a href={'/resources/studies/'+study.slug+'-record.json'} download>Download the structured study record</a><a data-prepare-inquiry data-prepare-kind='work-study' data-prepare-label='Design study' data-prepare-value={studyTitle(study)+' — '+study.question+' Illustrative website design work.'} href={inquiryHref}>Discuss this study with NRTH</a></div><div class='study-references'><h3>Follow the work</h3><ul>{study.references.map(reference=><li><a href={reference.href}>{reference.title}</a><p>{reference.note}</p></li>)}</ul></div><nav class='study-related-ventures' aria-label='Related NRTH perspectives'><span>Related venture perspectives</span>{study.ventures.map(slug=><a href={'/projects/'+slug}>{projects.find(project=>project.slug===slug)?.name||slug}</a>)}</nav></section>
 <WorkLibrary compact heading='Another question.<br/>Another perspective.'/>
</Layout>
<script>import '../scripts/work-library';</script>
